@attribute [CustomPage("Components/Overlays/Overview")]

<h1>Overlays</h1>

<h2><code>ChoiceSheet</code></h2>
<p>A <code>Sheet</code> that puts a two-way choice to the user: a message, a primary button and a destructive one under it. Closing it (scrim, Escape, back button) raises <code>OnClose</code> and the sheet stays open until the owner clears <code>Open</code>.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>Open</code>, <code>Title</code>, <code>Message</code>; <code>PrimaryText</code> with <code>OnPrimary</code>; <code>DangerText</code> with <code>OnDanger</code>; <code>OnClose</code>.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code> on the sheet, with <code>-scrim</code>, <code>-handle</code>, <code>-message</code>, <code>-primary</code> and <code>-danger</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2><code>ConfirmDialog</code></h2>
<p>A question over a scrim with a cancel and a confirm button. Cancel takes focus when it opens, and the Android back button raises <code>OnCancel</code>.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>Title</code> and optional <code>Message</code>; <code>ConfirmText</code> and <code>CancelText</code> (Cancel).</li>
    <li><code>Danger</code> styles the confirm button as destructive.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code> on the scrim, with <code>-cancel</code> and <code>-confirm</code> on the buttons.</li>
</ul>

<h2><code>Sheet</code></h2>
<p>A bottom sheet over a scrim, with a handle and a title that names it. It slides up (not with reduced motion) and is at most <code>--sheet-max-width</code> wide. Tab stays inside it (the topmost one, when sheets stack), and a tall body scrolls inside it up to <code>--sheet-max-height</code>. Focus returns to the element marked <code>data-sheet-opener</code> when there is one (the raised button of <code>AppScreen</code> and <code>BottomNav</code> takes it through their attributes), and otherwise to the control that had focus when the sheet opened. A tap on the scrim, Escape (also when focus has fallen to the page) and the Android back button raise <code>OnClose</code>; the sheet stays open until the owner clears <code>Open</code>.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>Open</code>, <code>Title</code> (heading and accessible name), <code>OnClose</code>, <code>ChildContent</code> for the body.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code> on the sheet, with <code>-scrim</code> and <code>-handle</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2><code>SheetAction</code></h2>
<p>A tile for a sheet's body: an icon over a label, at least a touch target tall. Put the tiles in a grid the sheet's body provides.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>Icon</code>, <code>Label</code>, <code>OnClick</code>; <code>TestId</code> on the button.</li>
</ul>

